From: latifangren <33740740+latifangren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kernel/module: allow vendor modules to load despite CRC differences

When adding container features (such as CONFIG_USER_NS and CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH),
the layout of core kernel structures changes, causing genksyms to generate
different CRC hashes for exported symbols such as module_layout.

Because pre-existing vendor modules in /vendor/lib/modules were compiled against
the stock kernel without these configs, strict check_version() rejects them
with "disagrees about version of symbol module_layout", leading to missing
hardware drivers (touchscreen, Wi-Fi) and bootloops.

Bypass the strict CRC rejection in check_version() by warning and returning 1,
allowing the kernel to load vendor modules seamlessly.
---
 kernel/module.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/module.c b/kernel/module.c
index 287f3b8..a4b2c1d 100644
--- a/kernel/module.c
+++ b/kernel/module.c
@@ -1249,7 +1249,7 @@ static int check_version(const struct load_info *info,
 
 bad_version:
 	pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s\n",
 	       info->name, symname);
-	return 0;
+	return 1;
 }
 
 static inline int check_modstruct_version(const struct load_info *info,
-- 
2.34.1
